# Campaign Naming Convention

When creating campaigns in Braze (via MCP tools, automation scripts, or any other method), **always** follow this naming convention. Campaign names in Asana tasks should also follow this convention.

## Pattern

```
[TYPE]_[CHANNEL]_[YYYY]_[MM]_[DD]_[BRAND]_[DESIGN]_[HAV_AUDIENCE?]_[CONTENT_TYPE?]_Description[_SUFFIX?]
```

All components use **underscores** as separators. Description words use **Title_Case**.

## Component Reference

### Campaign Type (required)
| Input | Code |
|-------|------|
| Promotional | P |
| Transactional | OT |
| CX | CX |
| Waitlist | WTL |
| Segmented | SEG |

### Channel (required)
| Input | Code |
|-------|------|
| Email | EM |
| SMS | SMS |
| Push | PUSH |

### Date (required)
Format: `YYYY_MM_DD` (e.g. `2026_02_10`)

### Brand (required)
| Brand | Code |
|-------|------|
| The Citizenry | CZ |
| St Frank | SF |
| Interior Define | ID |
| Havenly | HAV |
| The Inside | TI |
| Burrow | BW |
| Trade | TRADE |
| Cross-brand | ALL or TRADE_ALL or ALL_TRADE |

### Design Type (required for email, omit for SMS)
| Input | Code |
|-------|------|
| Designed | D |
| HTML | H |
| Plain-Text | PT |

### Havenly Audience (HAV only, required for HAV email campaigns)
| Input | Code |
|-------|------|
| Pre-Converted | PC |
| Converted | CONV |

### Content Type (optional)
| Input | Code |
|-------|------|
| Back in Stock | BIS |
| Color Story | CLR |
| Coming Soon | CS |
| Get the Look | GTL |
| Product Feature | PF |
| Ready to Ship | RTS |
| User Generated Content | UGC |
| At Risk | At_Risk |
| Cart Abandon | Cart_Abandon |
| Category Browse Abandon | Category_Browse |
| Delivery Confirmation | Delivery_Confirmation |
| Order Confirmation | Order_Confirmation |
| Out for Delivery | Out_for_Delivery |
| Post Purchase | Post_Purchase |
| Price Drop | Price_Drop |
| Product Browse Abandon | Product_Browse |
| Shipping Confirmation | Shipping_Confirmation |
| Waitlist | Waitlist |

### Description (required)
Free-form campaign description in Title_Case with underscores. E.g. `Winter_Sale_Reminder`, `Quick_Ship_Email`.

### Suffix (optional)
Common suffixes: `_PM`, `_AM`, `_EA` (Early Access), `_Retail`, `_Updated`, `_Resend`

## Examples by Brand

```
# Havenly — always include audience (PC or CONV)
P_EM_2026_02_10_HAV_D_PC_PF_Summer_Sale_Reminder
P_EM_2026_02_10_HAV_PT_CONV_Sale_Reminder
P_EM_2026_02_10_HAV_D_PC_GTL_Living_Room_Edit

# The Citizenry
P_EM_2026_01_29_CZ_D_Winter_Retreat_Sale_Last_Chance
P_EM_2026_01_23_CZ_D_Bath_Categories_PM

# Interior Define
P_EM_2026_01_29_ID_D_PF_Quick_Ship_Email
P_EM_2026_01_27_ID_PT_Winter_Retreat_Sale_Final_Hours

# Burrow
P_EM_2026_01_29_BW_D_City_Sized_Solutions
P_EM_2026_01_26_BW_PT_Stay_Warm_Shopping_PM

# Trade (cross-brand)
P_EM_2026_01_29_ALL_TRADE_PT_Appreciation_Week_Teaser
P_EM_2026_01_23_TRADE_ALL_D_Winter_Refresh_Sale_Reminder

# SMS (no design type needed)
P_SMS_2026_01_29_CZ_Winter_Retreat_Last_Chance
P_SMS_2026_01_27_BW_Sale_Final_Hours

# Transactional
OT_EM_2026_02_01_ID_D_Order_Confirmation
```

## Important Notes

- **PR is deprecated** — Do not include PR (Promo) in campaign names. Sale context is tracked via `data/sale_schedules.yaml` and the `sale_matcher` utility instead.
- **BW not BUR** — Burrow's Braze code is `BW`, not `BUR`. The YAML `brand` field uses `BUR` but the campaign name uses `BW`.
- **HAV audience is required** — Every Havenly email campaign must include PC or CONV after the design type.
- **SMS omits design type** — SMS campaigns go directly from brand to description.

## Utility Module

Use `scripts/utils/campaign_name.py` for programmatic name generation/validation:

```python
from scripts.utils.campaign_name import generate_campaign_name, validate_campaign_name

# Generate
name = generate_campaign_name(
    campaign_type="P",
    channel="EM",
    send_date="2026-02-10",
    brand="CZ",
    design_type="D",
    description="Winter Sale Launch",
)
# → "P_EM_2026_02_10_CZ_D_Winter_Sale_Launch"

# Validate
is_valid, issues = validate_campaign_name(name)
```

